{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
At the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]], the 32 teams were divided into eight groups of four, labelled A–H. Group C was composed of [[Saudi Arabia national football team|Saudi Arabia]], [[South Africa national football team|South Africa]], [[Denmark national football team|Denmark]] and host nation and eventual world champion [[France national football team|France]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/98full.html |title=World Cup 1998 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

Denmark and France started well, defeating Saudi Arabia and South Africa respectively. Next, France scored four to eliminate Saudi Arabia and qualify with a match to spare, while Denmark and South Africa drew. Needing a big win in their final game, against Saudi Arabia, South Africa conceded two penalties and could only draw, so Denmark still qualified despite losing their final game to France.

